- op: discuss  # cefa
  at: '2026-07-20T20:55:57Z'  # cefa
  by: agent  # cefa
  actor: jgstern_agent  # cefa
  clock: 3  # cefa
  nonce: cefa  # cefa
  message: "OWNER RULING 2026-07-20: Option C — refined predicate (reconcile both docs by subset). Direction set; leaving needs_human_review -> todo_hard for implementation.\n\nEMPIRICAL BASIS (fixture + real repo, noise-filter ON vs OFF via a temporary env-guard, reverted). entry_role=script is TWO populations the single predicate (kind==file and entry_role==script) cannot distinguish:\n  (1) npm package.json \"scripts\" (build/test/lint): kind=file lang=json, DEGREE-0 (no edges), concept=npm_script which detect_entrypoints does NOT recognize -> never detected as an entrypoint -> genuine noise. Filtering is CORRECT.\n  (2) pyproject [project.scripts] / cargo [[bin]] console-scripts: kind=file lang=toml, carries an outgoing defines_target(+calls) edge into the real CLI module, concept=pyproject_script which detect_entrypoints DOES recognize -> detected as CLI_COMMAND @0.99 evidence_type=manifest_declared -> genuine high-value entrypoint. Filtering WRONGLY drops it.\nEVIDENCE: synthetic fixture -> exempting scripts = +2 entrypoints (mycli/myworker @0.99), -0. Real repo beads-mcp -> current filter silently drops the package's SOLE declared CLI command (beads-mcp = \"beads_mcp.server:main\"); exempting recovers it (0.99 manifest_declared), loses nothing.\n\nRECONCILIATION (both governance docs STAND, each scoped to its correct subset — neither is overruled):\n  - audit-findings 0005 \"filter script as noise\" is CORRECT for the npm_script degree-0 subset.\n  - ADR-0043 §5 \"exempt entrypoint-bearing symbols (resolves C3)\" is CORRECT for the manifest-CLI subset — these ARE the entrypoint-bearing symbols the noise filter erases before detection (C3). The Wave-6 blanket fold over-corrected: it fixed the npm noise but re-opened C3 for pyproject/cargo CLI entrypoints.\nROOT CAUSE: a coarse predicate conflating \"degree-0 noise declaration\" with \"entrypoint-bearing manifest CLI\" — the same one-label-two-concepts pattern the correctness campaign targets.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION (cli.py + docs; none governance-locked): narrow _is_noise so it filters entry_role=script ONLY when the node is NOT entrypoint-bearing (the npm_script degree-0 case), and EXEMPTS the entrypoint-bearing case. Discriminator note: at filter time the pyproject_script CONCEPT is not yet on the node (resolved later in detection), so the discriminator must be filter-time-available — candidates in order of principledness: (a) reorder/exempt symbols that detection will flag as entrypoints (literally ADR-0043 §5's C3 intent); (b) meta.entry_point presence (pyproject sets it; npm run-scripts set meta.command, no entry_point); (c) presence of an outgoing defines_target edge. Then amend ADR-0043 §5 + audit-findings 0005 to state the subset boundary. TDD + own PR."  # cefa
