  clock: 5  # 288f
  nonce: 288f  # 288f
  message: "DONE — implemented Option C in PR #769 (merged fast-forward to dev). Root cause: the Phase-D noise filter treated every entry_role=script file symbol as noise (kind==file and entry_role==script), silently erasing entrypoint-bearing pyproject/console-scripts before detect_entrypoints ran (ADR-0043 §5 C3). Fix: extracted the predicate to the unit-testable noise_filter.is_noise_symbol and refined the script branch by meta['entry_point'] — bare npm run-scripts (meta['command'], no entry_point) filtered; entrypoint-bearing console-scripts (meta['entry_point']) exempt.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (closure-evidence discipline — this is a runtime/output-behavior item): (1) production-path regression test test_run_behavior_map.py::test_pyproject_console_script_survives_and_is_detected_wi_papag asserts the pyproject console-script survives the default filter AND is detected as a manifest_declared CLI_COMMAND, while npm run-scripts stay filtered — green in CI. (2) Live repro re-run: fixture with [project.scripts] -> exempting yields +2 CLI entrypoints (mycli/myworker @0.99), -0; real repo beads-mcp -> the sole declared CLI command (beads-mcp = beads_mcp.server:main) now survives and is detected (was silently dropped). Full suite 21097 passed / 100% coverage.\n\nGovernance reconciliation: amended ADR-0043 §5 (subset-refined exemption) and audit-findings 0005 (kind-fold does not mandate blanket noise-filtering) — both docs now stand, each scoped to its correct population. verify-generated recency trip on docs/ARCHITECTURE.md cleared by regeneration in the same PR (core modules 67->68 for the new noise_filter module)."  # 288f
